\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {S1}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Frozen $4\times 4$ compensated-core EP and matched control.} All panels use the rotated kernel of Eq.~(\ref {M-eq:Htilde}) at $k=0$ with $r=1$, $\tilde  {\epsilon }_{\xi }=-1$, fixed scalar hybridization $W=0.75$, and $G=\Gamma _{\rm  PT}=|\beta _0|$. The level $\tilde  {\epsilon }_{\xi }=-1$ is an assigned benchmark coefficient; the historical label $\epsilon _\xi =-U/2$ at $U=2$ is not an interaction calculation. No microscopic bath DOS, temperature or self-consistent filling enters. Panels (a)--(c) use the coherent splitting $D=\Delta _{\rm  eff}=0.50$. (a) Real and imaginary parts of all four eigenvalues. The exact local-core EPs are at $\beta _0=\pm 0.50$. (b) The Euclidean right-eigenvector condition number. The plotted spacing $\Delta \beta _0=0.0075$ places its nearest positive sample at $0.5025$, where $\kappa _{\rm  imp}=20.0304$; the exact origin remains $\kappa _{\rm  imp}(0)=1$. (c) Real part of the survival amplitude of main Sec.~\ref {M-sec:dynamics} below, at, and above the EP. Each trace is divided by its own maximum of $|{\rm  Re}\,O|$ on the window: $1.00$, $7.06$, and $1.79\times 10^4$ for $\beta _0=0.05$, $0.50$, and $0.75$. The normalized kernel contains the relative gain--loss but not the common width, so the amplitude grows linearly at the EP and exponentially above it; this growth belongs to the compensated representation and is not amplification by the passive physical kernel. Panels (d)--(f) repeat the same tests after switching off the coherent splitting ($D=0$); the divisors in (f) are $1.00$, $2.09$, and $12.9$. The smooth condition number in (e) and the traces in (f) form the relative-gain--loss-only control; they are not interpreted as a coherent impurity EP or as a Kondo-scale enhancement.}}{3}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:frozen_comparison}{{S1}{3}{\textbf {Frozen $4\times 4$ compensated-core EP and matched control.} All panels use the rotated kernel of Eq.~(\ref {M-eq:Htilde}) at $k=0$ with $r=1$, $\teps =-1$, fixed scalar hybridization $W=0.75$, and $G=\Gamma _{\rm PT}=|\beta _0|$. The level $\teps =-1$ is an assigned benchmark coefficient; the historical label $\epsilon _\xi =-U/2$ at $U=2$ is not an interaction calculation. No microscopic bath DOS, temperature or self-consistent filling enters. Panels (a)--(c) use the coherent splitting $D=\Delta _{\rm eff}=0.50$. (a) Real and imaginary parts of all four eigenvalues. The exact local-core EPs are at $\beta _0=\pm 0.50$. (b) The Euclidean right-eigenvector condition number. The plotted spacing $\Delta \beta _0=0.0075$ places its nearest positive sample at $0.5025$, where $\kappa _{\rm imp}=20.0304$; the exact origin remains $\kappa _{\rm imp}(0)=1$. (c) Real part of the survival amplitude of main Sec.~\ref {M-sec:dynamics} below, at, and above the EP. Each trace is divided by its own maximum of $|{\rm Re}\,O|$ on the window: $1.00$, $7.06$, and $1.79\times 10^4$ for $\beta _0=0.05$, $0.50$, and $0.75$. The normalized kernel contains the relative gain--loss but not the common width, so the amplitude grows linearly at the EP and exponentially above it; this growth belongs to the compensated representation and is not amplification by the passive physical kernel. Panels (d)--(f) repeat the same tests after switching off the coherent splitting ($D=0$); the divisors in (f) are $1.00$, $2.09$, and $12.9$. The smooth condition number in (e) and the traces in (f) form the relative-gain--loss-only control; they are not interpreted as a coherent impurity EP or as a Kondo-scale enhancement}{figure.1}{}}
